ITEM W — Coarse Height Provenance in Village Delta z
----------------------------------------------------
1. Code extract from run_mh_stats.py lines 121–125:
   Line 121:     dem = ee.Image('USGS/SRTMGL1_003').select('elevation')
   Line 122:     era5_proj = ee.ImageCollection('ECMWF/ERA5/DAILY').first().select(0).projection()
   Line 123:     dem_900 = dem.reduceResolution(reducer=ee.Reducer.mean(), maxPixels=65535).reproject(crs=era5_proj.crs(), scale=900)
   Line 124:     dem_e5 = dem_900.reduceResolution(reducer=ee.Reducer.mean(), maxPixels=65535).reproject(crs=era5_proj)
   Line 125:     abs_diff = dem.subtract(dem_e5).abs()

2. Categorization:
   - It is (b): SRTM reprojected/reduced to 0.25° and averaged via ee.Reducer.mean().
   - It is NOT ERA5 model spectral orography (geopotential_at_surface / 9.80665).
   - Therefore, Delta z measures DEM subgrid variance (30 m pixel fine elevation minus 0.25° cell-mean SRTM elevation),
     not the reanalysis model's internal orographic error.
   - Any statement that 'the forecast thinks the village is at X m' or claiming the coarse term is the model's orography
     is unsupported.


