ITEM AA — Verification of Measurement Flag 'D'
----------------------------------------------
1. Verbatim quote from data/cache/ghcnd-readme.txt line 312:
   'D     = precipitation total formed from four six-hour totals'
2. Correction of mechanism:
   - S assumed D meant 'multiday accumulation total / untagged missing recorded as zero'. That definition is WITHDRAWN.
   - Actual mechanism: Pre-2006 records were formed by aggregating four 6-hour synoptic reports (D,,S).
     Under 6-hour SYNOP reporting, missing transmission slots or operational dropouts produced an anomalous
     zero-day frequency of 39.7% in 1996–2003, compared to 14% post-2005.
3. Flag count distribution per season (from inspect_d_flag.py):
   - 1996: 35 D,,S | 62 ,,S (total 97)
   - 1998: 17 D,,S | 90 ,,S (total 107)
   - 2003: 19 D,,S | 92 ,,S (total 111)
   - 2004: 16 D,,S | 94 ,,S (total 110)
   - 2005: 12 D,,S | 94 ,,S (total 106)
   - 2006–2019 (all 9 remaining valid seasons): 0 D,,S | 100% ,,S
4. Max daily 55.1 mm in 1996 and 2003:
   - 1996-06-19: 55.1 mm (551 tenths of mm)
   - 2003-06-22: 55.1 mm (551 tenths of mm)
   - Single date occurrence per season; numerical coincidence, not an artificial ceiling clipping. Pos values reach 98 mm (2007) and 148 mm (2019).


